---
/**
 * EdgePattern — the brand's metaball motif at the right edge of a full-bleed
 * band (bundle components/hero/Hero): one full-strength instance hugging the
 * viewport edge, one tonal instance below it. Shared by the home hero and
 * /registration so the two are the same element by construction (Issue #90) —
 * the owner rejected a registration-only variant as «не как на главной».
 *
 * Contract for the host band: it is full-bleed, `position: relative` and
 * clips its overflow (that clip is what keeps the pattern from creating
 * horizontal scroll); its content wrapper is a positioned sibling rendered
 * AFTER this component, so the copy and any opaque panel paint above it.
 *
 * The artwork MUST stay inlined through this import: the asset ships
 * `fill="currentColor"` so its colour is a token (`.ob-edge-pattern`), and the
 * design bundle renders it as `<img src=…>` — porting that verbatim would paint
 * a silent BLACK metaball, because `currentColor` in a referenced SVG never
 * sees this page. Decorative, so hidden from assistive tech; rendered from lg
 * upwards only (see the CSS).
 */
import Metaball from '@/assets/metaball-element.svg';
---

<Metaball class="ob-edge-pattern ob-edge-pattern--a" aria-hidden="true" />
<Metaball class="ob-edge-pattern ob-edge-pattern--b" aria-hidden="true" />
